/*
 * syscall.h.in - syscall numbers.  OVMX alpha-dec-vms musl port (vms-960).
 *
 * ==========================================================================
 * AUTHORITATIVE ALPHA NUMBERING (vms-157): every value below is the real
 * OSF/1-derived Alpha syscall number, dumped from the Linux-Alpha toolchain's
 * <asm/unistd.h> (alpha-linux-gnu, the OVMX/Linux-Alpha lane oracle) -- NOT
 * transcribed from memory. The syscall backend (src/internal/vms_alpha_syscall,
 * now a real callsys trap) puts this number in $0 and traps to the Linux-Alpha
 * kernel, so these MUST match the kernel's table exactly. The name set is
 * unchanged from the rung-1 placeholder file (every SYS_* musl references still
 * resolves); only the values are corrected. newfstatat maps to Alpha fstatat64
 * (455): musl aliases SYS_fstatat->SYS_newfstatat. kexec_file_load has no Alpha
 * number (unreferenced by musl) and keeps its inert placeholder.
 *
 * (This comment deliberately avoids the N-R token: the musl Makefile greps this
 * file for that token to derive the SYS_* names, so any prose use would leak a
 * broken line into the generated bits/syscall.h.)
 * ==========================================================================
 */
